.TH DEOPJUFY 1 "2026-08-21" "deopjufy 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deopjufy \- inspect and extract content from Origin OPJ and OPJU projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deopjufy
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
.B deopjufy inspect
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B deopjufy list
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-exhaustive ]
.RB [ \-\-include\-raw\-gaps ]
.PP
.B deopjufy get
.I FILE ITEM_ID
.RB [ \-\-format " FORMAT" ]
.RB [ \-o " OUTPUT" ]
.PP
.B deopjufy extract
.I FILE
.B \-o
.I OUTDIR
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
.B deopjufy strings
.I FILE
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
.B deopjufy images
.I FILE
.RB [ \-o " OUTDIR" ]
.PP
.B deopjufy table-scan
.I FILE
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
.B deopjufy walk
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B deopjufy dump-block
.I FILE
.B \-\-offset
.I N
.B \-\-length
.I N
.PP
.B deopjufy compare
.I LEFT RIGHT
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-compare\-bytes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deopjufy
is a deterministic, native-only Unix utility for recovering inspectable content
from Origin project files. It does not require Origin, Wine, R, an external
parser, a viewer, a remote service, or network access during extraction.
.PP
OPJ and OPJU support is intentionally partial and corpus-scoped. Parser-backed,
heuristic, partial, unsupported, and exactly verified results remain distinct in
machine output. An artifact being written is not proof that every related source
object or every byte-level semantic field was decoded.
.PP
Single-stream command output is written to standard output. Diagnostics and
warnings are written to standard error. Multi-file extraction writes only below
an explicitly selected output directory and records the result in
.IR manifest.json .
.SH DISCLAIMER
This software is vibe-coded, use it carefully for one-off tasks.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS inspect
Report detected type, input size and digest, parser status, support class,
coverage scope, and warnings.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the stable machine-readable representation instead of human output.
.SS list
List discoverable catalog items, their source evidence, and supported retrieval
formats. JSON catalog schema version 1 supplies deterministic opaque item IDs
bound to the exact input digest.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the versioned catalog JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-exhaustive
Disable the normal OPJU heuristic-kind cap.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-raw\-gaps
Include uncovered source ranges as
.B raw_gap
items.
.SS get
Materialize one item identified by an ID from
.BR "list --json" .
IDs must not be parsed or reused after the input bytes change.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Select
.BR json ,
.BR jsonl ,
.BR csv ,
.BR tsv ,
.BR xlsx ,
.BR bmp ,
.BR gif ,
.BR jpeg ,
.BR jpg ,
.BR png ,
or
.BR svg .
The catalog item's
.B retrieval_formats
field is authoritative.
.TP
.BI \-o " OUTPUT"
Write the primary artifact to this file. Without this option, JSON retrieval is
written to standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the complete schema-version-1 retrieval envelope.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Permit replacement of an existing output file.
.SS extract
Recover recognized content into a new directory and write
.IR manifest.json .
Possible outputs include tables, matrices, notes, functions, report records,
images, attachments, graph metadata or stored previews, semantic provenance,
raw regions, and an exact reconstructable byte map. Availability depends on
input evidence.
.TP
.BI \-o " OUTDIR"
Select the extraction directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Write tabular artifacts as
.BR csv ,
.BR tsv ,
.BR json ,
or optional
.BR xlsx .
.TP
.BI \-\-manifest " PATH"
Select a manifest path.
.TP
.BI \-\-raw\-dir " PATH"
Select the raw-region directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-raw\-min\-bytes " N"
Set the minimum raw-region size; the default is 1024.
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-dir " PATH"
Select the carved-text directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-min\-bytes " N"
Set the minimum carved-text source size; the default is 1024.
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-min\-length " N"
Set the minimum text run length; the default is 4.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-images ,
.BR \-\-no\-strings ,
.BR \-\-no\-tables ,
.B \-\-no\-objects
Disable the corresponding extraction family.
.TP
.B \-\-parser\-only
Disable heuristic object discovery and collection.
.TP
.BR \-\-human ,
.BR \-\-human\-only ,
.BR \-\-human\-artifacts\-only ,
.BR \-\-extended ,
.B \-\-map
Select one extraction profile. See
.BR deopjufy-manifest (5).
.TP
.BI \-\-strings\-min\-length " N"
Set the printable-string threshold; the default is 4.
.TP
.BI \-\-table\-min\-rows " N"
Set the heuristic table row threshold; the default is 1 for extraction.
.TP
.BI \-\-table\-min\-columns " N"
Set the heuristic table column threshold; the default is 2.
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on\-partial
Return status 4 when a required result remains partial.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Permit replacement of existing extraction targets.
.SS strings
Print visible text strings from the input.
.TP
.BI \-\-encoding " ENCODING"
Select
.BR ascii ,
.BR utf16 ,
.BR latin1 ,
or
.BR utf-8 .
The default is ASCII.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-length " N"
Set the minimum run length; the default is 4.
.TP
.B \-\-decoded
Scan parser-decoded OPJU LZ4 payloads instead of raw file bytes. This mode is
OPJU-only.
.SS images
Carve validated embedded image signatures into an output directory.
.TP
.BI \-o " OUTDIR"
Select the image directory.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a machine-readable extraction report.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Permit replacement of existing files.
.SS table-scan
Heuristically scan for numeric tables. This command is separate from
parser-owned worksheet extraction and must not be treated as confirmed project
structure.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-rows " N"
Set the minimum row count; the default is 5.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-columns " N"
Set the minimum column count; the default is 2.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Select
.BR csv ,
.BR tsv ,
or
.BR json .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the command report as JSON.
.SS walk
Report parser-known records and exact or qualified source ranges.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable output.
.SS dump-block
Copy exactly the requested input range to standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-offset " N"
Set the zero-based input offset.
.TP
.BI \-\-length " N"
Set the byte count.
.SS compare
Compare two extraction directories or manifest files.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable differences.
.TP
.B \-\-compare\-bytes
Also compare extracted artifact bytes.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the installed version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable detailed diagnostics for commands that support verbosity.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress non-error diagnostics for commands that support quiet mode.
.SH OUTPUT CONTRACT
Extraction paths are sanitized, relative to the selected output root, and never
escape it. Existing user data is not overwritten without
.BR \-\-force .
.PP
Every directory extraction writes a manifest, including partial runs. Unknown
bytes can be preserved by machine profiles. Complete byte reconstruction proves
source-byte coverage, not semantic understanding. See
.BR deopjufy-manifest (5)
and
.BR deopjufy-formats (7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command usage.
.TP
.B 3
Unsupported input or required feature.
.TP
.B 4
Partial extraction with
.BR \-\-fail\-on\-partial .
.TP
.B 5
Requested optional dependency unavailable.
.TP
.B 6
Corrupted or truncated input.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
deopjufy inspect project.opju
deopjufy list project.opju --json
deopjufy get project.opju ITEM_ID --format csv -o sheet.csv
deopjufy extract project.opju -o output/
deopjufy extract project.opju -o complete/ --map
deopjufy dump-block project.opju --offset 4096 --length 1024 > block.bin
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I manifest.json
Machine-readable extraction record.
.TP
.I tables/, matrices/, notes/, images/, metadata/, provenance/, raw/, byte-map/
Conventional extraction subdirectories, emitted only when applicable.
.PP
The CLI creates no persistent application cache, recent-file list, project
database, or hidden network state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR deopjufy-view (1),
.BR deopjufy-manifest (5),
.BR deopjufy-formats (7)
